        //
        // However, we also have other favorites we are not pushing; they might also
        // compete. But we don't care about them; we only care that our 'mid' favorites
        // are in top K. So the threshold is: the minimum vote among the top K after allocation.
        // If we push 'mid' favorites, the other K-mid spots go to the highest non-favorites
        // (assuming no other favorites surpass them). So each pushed favorite must have
        // final votes > the (K-mid)-th highest non-favorite (or >=, but careful with ties).
