                // the top K will include all non-favorites and some favorites. The threshold is
                // the minimum vote among those top K. To guarantee our pushed favorites are in,
                // they need to be > the (need - nonFav.size())-th favorite? This gets complicated.
                // Let's simplify: If need > nonFav.size(), then threshold = 0, because we can
                // always put our favorites above the non-favorites easily. But we must ensure
                // they beat other favorites? Actually, if need > nonFav.size(), then there are
                // more spots than non-favorites, so some favorites will automatically be in top K
                // even with 0 votes? No, votes are given. The threshold is the K-th highest vote.
